[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Combat/Actions/ActionDefinitionResource.cs" id="4_action"]

; The Ashen Knight's fight (the finish run, Act IV). Modelled on data/bosses/IronKing.tres and harder
; on every axis, and a DUEL: there are no adds at all. The Knight is the one Flamebearer who would
; think it beneath him to need help.
;
;   phase 1  the fencer. Cut, cut, thrust off his greatsword; the cuts can be staggered.
;   phase 2  at 66%: faster, and his wind-ups are harder to break (poise x0.7). The punish window
;            is still there; it is shorter.
;   phase 3  at 33%: HE STOPS FENCING. A new move set — a gap-closing lunge and a whirling cut, both
;            uninterruptible — and nothing in it can be traded with. The answer becomes the dodge.
;
; A long enrage (4 minutes) forces phase three: a rival does not let you wait him out.

